  "adaptation": {
    "semantic": "The difference between bare **little** (not enough) and **a little** (a small but real amount) has no equivalent in some languages, where one word covers both; the article carries the meaning in English.",
    "grammar": "**Little** and **a little** go only with uncountable nouns; the equivalent for countable plural nouns is **few** and **a few**.",
